<title>RUSSIA: Russian grain harvest two-thirds complete.</title>
<headline>Russian grain harvest two-thirds complete.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia had harvested 65 percent of its grain crops, excluding maize, and threshed 49.5 million tonnes bunker weight as of September 2, the state statistics committee said on Monday.</p>
<p>It released the following data:</p>
<p>			    PACE OF RUSSIAN GRAIN HARVEST</p>
<p>					  AS OF SEPT 2</p>
<p>				  1996    1995	  1994</p>
<p>Cut (excl. maize, in million hectares)</p>
<p>				  31.2    32.9	  27.0</p>
<p>  as pct of sown area     65	67	    54</p>
<p>Threshed</p>
<p>  (million hectares)	29.6    31.4	  23.9</p>
<p>(million tonnes, bunker weight)</p>
<p>				  49.5    45.4	  47.2</p>
<p>  as pct of sown area     62	64	    48</p>
<p>  as pct of cut area	95	96	    89</p>
<p> Yield (tonnes/hectare)   1.67    1.45	  1.98</p>
<p>-- Lynnley Browning, Moscow Newsroom +7095 941 8520</p>
